                                        <height>1,145</height>
                                        <width>58,8</width>
                                        <depth></depth>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout>
                                    <p>Stele in 14 fragments with pediment, acroteria, dentils, two Corinthian columns. Main field shows two crescents at top and bull tied to flaming altar at bottom. Dedicated by Marcus Virrius Genokios Antonianus and Marcus Virrius Genokios Sanctos Antonianus to Men Patrios.</p>
                                    <rs ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1">incisa a scalpello</rs>
